Types of Hypervisor:
Type 1 (Bare-Metal) Hypervisor: Runs directly on the host hardware, without a host operating system (OS).
ex: VMWare, Xen
Type 2 (Hosted) Hypervisor: Runs as an application on top of a conventional host operating system (like Windows, macOS, or Linux).
ex: Oracle VM VirtualBox

